{"id": "EUVD-2026-99008", "enisaUuid": "ecddb0df-6e39-3c25-91aa-63fc31a0f78b", "description": "Kavita 0.9.0 through 0.9.1.4 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows authenticated users to bypass the SSRF blocklist through DNS rebinding or HTTPS redirects. Attackers can submit a URL to POST /api/Cbl/upload-cbl-file whose host rebinds or redirects to internal addresses after validation, enabling blind internal port and service probing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:57:31", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/kavita-cbl-url-preflight-ssrf", "https://github.com/Kareadita/Kavita/blob/879b8b73eb41d66f88dde8eb874cc99a3397eb11/Kavita.Server/Controllers/CBLController.cs#L82-L108", "https://github.com/Kareadita/Kavita/blob/879b8b73eb41d66f88dde8eb874cc99a3397eb11/Kavita.Common/Helpers/FlurlConfiguration.cs#L46-L89", "https://github.com/Kareadita/Kavita", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/kavita-0.9.0-through-0.9.1.4-ssrf-blocklist-bypass-via-upload-cbl-file-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r6xw-vr9q-6g8x", "CVE-2026-110223"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "393f1d9d-e4c9-3528-b47a-4682e34ca291", "product": {"name": "Kavita", "vendor": {"name": "kareadita"}}, "product_version": "0.9.0 \u22640.9.1.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b5ee7066-a3e8-3d99-ad3b-bd524e243765", "vendor": {"name": "kareadita"}}], "isExploited": false}